@startuml deployment
title Local stack - docker compose, ten services

skinparam shadowing false

actor Client
actor Developer

node "docker compose network" {
  node "individuals-api\nhost 8081 -> 8081" as API
  node "keycloak\nhost 8080 -> 8080" as KC
  database "keycloak-postgres\nhost 5433 -> 5432" as KCDB
  database "person-postgres\nhost 5434 -> 5432" as PSDB
  node "nexus\nhost 8083 -> 8081" as NEXUS
  node "prometheus\nhost 9090 -> 9090" as PROM
  node "alloy\nhost 12345 -> 12345" as ALLOY
  database "loki\nhost 3100 -> 3100" as LOKI
  database "tempo\nhost 3200, 4318" as TEMPO
  node "grafana\nhost 3000 -> 3000" as GRAF
}

node "person-service\n8082 - arrives in module 2" as PS

Client --> API : POST /api/v1/auth/...
API --> KC : Admin REST API\nand OIDC token endpoint
API ..> PS : HTTP, not running yet
KC --> KCDB : JDBC

PROM --> API : scrape /actuator/prometheus
ALLOY --> API : read stdout\nvia the Docker socket
ALLOY --> LOKI : push
API --> TEMPO : OTLP push /v1/traces

GRAF --> PROM
GRAF --> LOKI
GRAF --> TEMPO

Developer --> NEXUS : ./gradlew :person-client:publish
API ..> NEXUS : resolved at build time,\nnever at run time

note right of PROM
  Prometheus pulls, the application pushes.
  That is why the app address lives in
  prometheus.yml while the Tempo address
  lives in application.yml.
end note

note bottom of NEXUS
  Not on any runtime path. The Gradle build
  on the host publishes person-client here and
  resolves it by Maven coordinates - which is
  what keeps modules from depending on each
  other through project(":...").

  Port 8083 because the handout gives 8081
  to individuals-api, so Nexus is the one
  that moves off its own default.
end note

note bottom of PSDB
  Runs in module 1 only so the Flyway
  migrations have something to apply to.
  Nothing connects to it yet.
end note

note right of ALLOY
  Needed because the application writes to
  stdout and Docker keeps that in a file that
  dies with the container. The Loki docker
  driver would have done it too, but it is a
  host plugin - and "docker compose up brings
  everything up" is an acceptance criterion.
end note

@enduml
